# Where the landing page's "Get Started" / "Launch" CTA points: the console's
# sign-UP screen. Someone arriving from a marketing page usually does not have
# an account yet; AuthView's own "already have an account?" switch covers the
# other direction in one click. A plain cross-origin link on purpose -- the two apps are separate
# builds on separate origins with no cross-origin token handoff, which is what
# lets them ship independently. Do not turn this into a shared session.
#
# localhost, NOT 127.0.0.1. The repo-wide "127.0.0.1, never localhost" rule is
# about the browser-to-uvicorn hop. Neon Auth rejects http://127.0.0.1:<port> as
# an untrusted origin, so a console served from the IP literal fails every
# sign-up. See apps/console/AGENTS.md.
VITE_CONSOLE_URL=http://localhost:5175/auth/sign-up
